+# Perf history
+
+## SessionStart health gate
+
+Checked git history for `crates/muninn-core/src/health.rs`, `db.rs`, `schema.sql`
+(the files that hold `quick_check`, the `fts_rows` counter, and the `body` CHECK
+constraint). Only two commits ever touch them: `2ff626a` (Phase 0, the repo's
+first commit) and later additive commits. `2ff626a` is the root commit — there
+is no earlier revision.
+
+In `2ff626a`, the SessionStart hook path (`live=false` in `health::run`) already
+reads only the recorded `quick_check_result` from `meta`, plus the `fts_rows`
+counter; `schema.sql` already has the `body` CHECK constraint. So "quick_check
+on the read path, no `fts_rows` counter, no `body` CHECK" is not a state this
+repo ever had — I can't find a measured p50 for it, because it never existed.
+
+No measured p50 for a 5k-record store, before or after, is on record in this
+worktree (`docs/`, `research/`) either. `muninn-bench perf` (default 5000
+records) can produce one, but running it here requires `cargo build --release`,
+which needs approval this session didn't get.
+
+**Numbers in this section are TODO, not estimates.** Run:
+
+```
+cargo build --release -p muninn-bench
+./target/release/muninn-bench perf
+```
+
+and record the `hook SessionStart` p50 line here.
